35	- `FND-0020` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: R^1 pi_* Q for the universal n-punctured curve is mixed of weights 1 and 2 (an extension of a rank n-1 Tate system of weight 2 by the rank 2g weight-1 system), never pure of weight 1. The correct weight floor is therefore H^p(base;L) of weight >= p+1, so at p=2d-k-1 the relevant graded piece is Gr^W_{p+1}, and any 'W_p' group named at that spot is identically zero. Attempts that describe the punctured-curve system as pure of weight 1 will be off by exactly one unit of weight and will target a zero group. ATT-0011 exhibits this error in section 2 while stating the correct description in section 5.
36	- `FND-0022` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: A gonality or Brill-Noether stratification of M_{g,n-1} does not by itself bound the pure-weight cohomology of a local system on the total space: one needs the localization spectral sequence with the correct codimension shifts and Tate twists (in genus 6 the hyperelliptic locus has codimension 4 in M_6, contributing via degree p-8 cohomology of the stratum twisted by Q(-4)) together with control of its differentials. Evaluating only the open stratum is insufficient, since restriction to it is in general neither injective nor surjective. ATT-0011 supplies no shift, twist, or differential bookkeeping, and its stratification is additionally mislabelled: for g=6 gonality takes only values 2, 3, 4, the posited residual Brill-Noether strata are not separate gonality strata, and the gonality-4 open contains the Brill-Noether-special plane quintic locus.
37	- `FND-0031` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: In the Deligne weight spectral sequence of (Mbar_{g,n}, boundary), the corner gr^W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n}) computing the RED-0001 open input sits at spectral-sequence depth m = weight - degree = 0. Hence only the m=0 term H^{2d-16}(Mbar_{g,n}) and the single d_1 Gysin map from the codimension-one strata H^{2d-18}(D^{(1)})(-1) can contribute; strata of codimension >= 2, multi-edge stable graphs, and higher differentials (E_2-degeneration) are all irrelevant to this corner. Dualizing, the resulting cokernel is identical to the boundary sequence of THM-0003, so the weight spectral sequence and the Getzler-Kapranov graph complex yield no information beyond THM-0003 at this corner and cannot break the circularity: they express the open input in terms of the still-unknown H^{16}(Mbar_{g,n}). Any attempt of this approach type must add an independent input for the m=0 term or attack a different corner.
38	- `FND-0032` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The CGP / tropical-moduli / commutative-graph-complex computation controls gr^W_0 H^*_c(M_{g,n}), equivalently the top-weight piece gr^W_{2d}H^*(M_{g,n}), whereas the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} = gr^W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n})(d) is the LOWEST weight in its degree (H^{2d-16} of a smooth d-fold has weights in [2d-16, 2d]). The two corners coincide only when 2d = 2d-16, i.e. never. For (6,6), d=21: CGP computes weight 42, the target is weight 26. No twist or dimension-shift bookkeeping can reconcile them, so 'match the CGP degree index to the target' is not an unwritten reference chain but an impossible identification; the undecorated top-weight regime is never the surviving corner for any pair in RED-0001.
39	- `FND-0033` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: The RED-0001 target W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}) is a PURE polarizable Q-Hodge structure of weight -16, and the entire weight-(2d-16) row of the E_1 page is pure of that single weight. Since polarizable pure Q-Hodge structures of a fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category, any subquotient of a direct sum of Tate objects in that row is again a direct sum of the same Tate object. Consequently there is no non-split-extension obstruction and no semisimplification-versus-actual-isomorphism gap in this corner: proving Tate type on the associated graded of the contributing terms is already an honest Hodge-structure isomorphism. Attempts should not spend a gap marker on ruling out exotic extensions here, and reviewers should not credit such a gap as substantive.
40	- `FND-0034` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: For (g,n)=(6,6) the non-separating boundary divisor has normalization Mbar_{5,8}, not Mbar_{5,7} as ATT-0014 states: the genus drops by one and the normalization gains TWO legs at the node, 6+2=8, and dim Mbar_{5,8} = 3*5-3+8 = 20 = 21-1 confirms codimension one while dim Mbar_{5,7} = 19 does not. This matters beyond arithmetic: combined with the depth-one restriction above, the only Gysin source into H^{26}(Mbar_{6,6}) other than separating-divisor products is Mbar_{5,8}, and (5,8) is itself an unresolved pair in RED-0001. Any depth-one attack on (6,6) therefore couples directly to the (5,8) case rather than to strictly simpler discharged inputs, and the correct edge-decorated E_1 term is (H^*(Mbar_Gamma) tensor det E_Gamma)^{Aut(Gamma)} -- the determinant twist on the edge set, omitted by ATT-0014, kills contributions whose automorphisms permute edges oddly or swap the two branches of the non-separating node.
