63	- `FND-0071` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: A low-degree diagonal statement that, at 2r=2g+n-2, only the kernel of restriction H^{2r}(\overline{M}_{g,n})→H^{2r}(D) is Tate does not by itself make the whole group H^{2r}(\overline{M}_{g,n}) Tate; boundary-supported classes and the full stratified contribution must still be controlled.
64	- `FND-0072` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}}]: No complete unconditional proof that H^{16}(\overline{M}_{6,6};Q) is a direct sum of Q(-8) is supplied by ATT-0027; graph-complex/arc-contraction slogans without Aut-invariants, Gysin shifts, differentials, and higher-genus primitives do not discharge this.
